      "writtenOn": "2024-12-10T23:34:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi. LL-NDK is kind of a weird place because it\u0027s reviewed by NDK API review in order to keep map txt files simple, and to keep C review consistent, but the deadlines are set by ANAPIC for vendors. We need to combine things/processes and avoid splitting the code up, to reduce complexity in Android.\n\nSo to confirm, from this thread:\n- this is not an API for apps, so it should follow HAL dates, not API dates.\n- from a technical perspective, this must happen before VINTF finalization.\n- ANAPIC has already okay\u0027d this API addition, since partners need it based on direct meetings w/ partners. We made an exception for this case, since the alternative impact to security policies and AVF is not acceptable.\n\nInseob: we should button up the LL-NDK here and get any last changes in. Can you confirm this is the last change? or the whole scope? Please add to commit message as well.\n\nYurii/Eino-Ville: this has come up for a few years running, please let me know if you want to discuss more or formalize things, we can do a joint NDK/ANAPIC meeting, add an LL-NDK person to the NDK meetings, or well yeah maybe this makes sense, let me know if there is anything else we need to follow up here.",
